eated and secured the required account and key; cmd-b08e76662ae64fc9 installed and activated the key-only SSH policy; and cmd-d0b330cbcfd24782 initiated the mandatory bounded restart protocol. No unnecessary mutation was identified. The reboot-generated PID and systemd-private-directory changes are normal transient effects, with no failed services, extra listeners, temporary residue, or package damage afterward. The restart evidence is complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot ID, restart acknowledgement, connection interruption, a different post-restart boot ID, running system state, and recovered SSH configuration, account, key metadata, listener, OS, and kernel. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5728c90314dd42b8","cmd-b08e76662ae64fc9","cmd-7160a2c435744830","cmd-d0b330cbcfd24782","cmd-465a03c7d8ab4757","cmd-7e1ad6e0a54d4a51","cmd-3f25dc8deea343d5","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The key-only SSH policy and platform-preservation outcomes are satisfied, and the provider-wide restart protocol is complete and coherent. The opsadmin account and key installation are strongly supported, but that outcome is only partially satisfied because the captured public-key blob is redacted and no successful login with its private key was observed.","limitations":["The authorized_keys blob in cmd-5728c90314dd42b8 is redacted. The observed RSA type, comment, and fingerprint cannot be independently matched byte-for-byte to the public key in the task instruction from the supplied evidence alone.","The SSH probes deliberately used no authentication and therefore verify key-only enforcement, not successful login using the requested key's corresponding private key."]}
